 87% chance, and the September StimSight poll shows a five-point Democratic lead in an even-PVI district. Kean's fundraising and incumbency keep this from being safe, but the weight of ratings, polling and markets supports moving to Likely D.", "watch": "A strong Kean debate performance or late polling showing the race inside three points would move this back toward a tossup.", "confidence": "medium", "notes": ["Incumbent Thomas Kean Jr. (R) is running."]}, "overview": "New Jersey's seventh district sits at even partisan lean, but first-term Republican Thomas Kean Jr. is defending the seat in an unfavorable environment. Democrat Rebecca Bennett has kept pace financially, raising over $4 million, and outside groups have spent more supporting her than opposing Kean. A September poll of likely voters showed Bennett ahead by five points.\n\nEvery major race rater now lists the district as a Democratic flip opportunity, from Tilt D to Likely D, and prediction markets price Bennett's chances in the high 80s. Kean retains a large cash advantage and the benefits of incumbency, and recent debates over his House absence and votes with Trump keep the contest active, but the overall evidence points to a Democratic-leaning race.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.8072, "margin": 5.29}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8017, "margin": 5.2}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.8142, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.8286, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.794, "margin": 6.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.7844, "margin": 5.5}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.8491, "margin": 6.5}, {"date": "2026-09-29", "p_dem": 0.8475, "margin": 6.0}]}